#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Adds audio geolocation (README_audio_geolocation.md) to the EDTH repo.

Run it from the EDTH folder (the one with start.sh in it):

    python install_audio_geolocation.py

It writes the new backend/app/geo/ package and tests, and updates the files that plug it in (dev_server.py,
voice.py, roads.py, repo.py, turing_repo.py, messages.py, the dashboard and the docs). Built against main
at fb61ee6.

Safe to run: a file is only replaced if it is exactly what it was at fb61ee6. If a teammate has changed one
since, it is left alone and the new version is saved beside it as <name>.geo-new for you to merge.
Every replaced file is backed up under .geo-backup/. Run it twice and the second run does nothing.

    python install_audio_geolocation.py --undo     put the backed-up files back and remove the new ones
"""
